{
  "title": "Fewest Slices Into Mirror Pieces",
  "description": "## Task\n\nCut `s` into consecutive pieces so that every piece reads the same forwards and backwards. Return the smallest number of pieces that makes this possible. A single character is always such a piece.\n\n## Input\n\n- `s` — a string of lowercase letters. It may be empty.\n\n## Output\n\nThe minimum number of pieces. An empty string needs `0` pieces.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\nmin_mirror_pieces(\"aab\")  # returns 2  (\"aa\" + \"b\")\nmin_mirror_pieces(\"racecar\")  # returns 1\nmin_mirror_pieces(\"abc\")  # returns 3\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 0 ≤ length of `s` ≤ 2000\n- `s` contains only the lowercase letters `a`-`z`.\n- Trying every possible set of cuts is far too slow for the largest inputs.\n",
  "signature": "def min_mirror_pieces(s: str) -> int",
  "topic": "palindrome partition dp",
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "category": "strings",
  "tests": [
    { "args": ["aab"], "expected": 2 },
    { "args": ["racecar"], "expected": 1 },
    { "args": ["abc"], "expected": 3 },
    { "args": [""], "expected": 0 },
    { "args": ["a"], "expected": 1 },
    { "args": ["abba"], "expected": 1 },
    { "args": ["aaaaaaaa"], "expected": 1 },
    { "args": [""], "expected": 2 },
    { "args": [""], "expected": 1950 },
    { "args": [""], "expected": 275 },
    { "args": [""], "expected": 1781 }
  ]
}
